# Git Conventions

## Overview
Conventional commits format for Git commit messages following the Conventional Commits specification. This rule ensures consistent commit message formatting across the workspace.

## Basic Conventions
Implement conventional commits using Conventional commits. You can use the doc you already have registered.

## Rules

Based on that conventions the git commit message should have the following format:

```
feat(microservices-shared): whatever the message is.
```

You can get the available projects from Nx.

